<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-023/1> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "achieving an accuracy of 0.673 on the ADHD-200 holdout data and 0.643 on the ABIDE holdout data. Both of these results, obtained with the same LEFMSF framework, are the best known, over all hold-out accuracies on these datasets when only using imaging data—exceeding previously-published results by 0.012 for ADHD and 0.042 for Autism." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_0a18ed38 full_text sha256:c45b568564aed9a2ce5c1559ce50c6a119000557051d641a0d3cc5a393d3dcae section:abstract (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "The combined structural+functional learner (LEFMSF) achieves 0.643 hold-out accuracy on ABIDE, the best known result using imaging data alone at the time, exceeding prior work by 0.042." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-023/2> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "The ABIDE dataset consists of 1111 scans, taken from 17 sites consisting of 573 healthy controls and 538 patients with autism. To evaluate each learning model, we use 800 subjects (70%) for model training and 311 subjects (30%) for hold-out testing. We use the same case/control ratio (0.5157) for both training and test set." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_0a18ed38 full_text sha256:c45b568564aed9a2ce5c1559ce50c6a119000557051d641a0d3cc5a393d3dcae section:methods (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "ABIDE: 1111 scans from 17 sites (573 HC, 538 ASD), split 800 (70%) training / 311 (30%) hold-out test, preserving the case:control ratio in both sets." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-023/3> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "For preprocessing fMRI and MRI scans, we used SPM8 (http://www.fil.ion.ucl.ac.uk/spm/ software/spm8/) and our own in-house MATLAB code. Preprocessing was identical to that used in Ghiassian et al. [13]." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_0a18ed38 full_text sha256:c45b568564aed9a2ce5c1559ce50c6a119000557051d641a0d3cc5a393d3dcae section:methods (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "Preprocessing used SPM8 plus in-house MATLAB code, identical to a prior published pipeline (Ghiassian et al.)." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-023/4> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "the resulting hold-out accuracy for ADHD was 0.6491 (baseline 0.5497) and was 0.6233 for ABIDE (baseline 0.5157). The specificity, sensitivity and Jstat for ADHD (resp., ABIDE) are 0.8191, 0.4416 and 0.2607 (respectively, 0.6768, 0.5533 and 0.2301). To our knowl- edge, our holdout accuracies achieved on ADHD-200 test data and the ABIDE test data are the best known when only using fMRI scans." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_0a18ed38 full_text sha256:c45b568564aed9a2ce5c1559ce50c6a119000557051d641a0d3cc5a393d3dcae section:results (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "Hold-out accuracy was 0.6233 for ABIDE (baseline 0.5157), described as the best known result using fMRI scans alone." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-023/5> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "We found that models trained using only site information achieved an accuracy of 66.0% on the ADHD data and 55.0% on the ABIDE data, while our models trained on MRI data achieved much higher accuracies: 67.4% and 64.3%, respectively." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_0a18ed38 full_text sha256:c45b568564aed9a2ce5c1559ce50c6a119000557051d641a0d3cc5a393d3dcae section:results (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "A model using only site identity achieved just 55.0% accuracy on ABIDE, far below the 64.3% achieved using MRI-derived features, indicating the classifier is not simply exploiting site identity." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-023/6> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "We then tested those previously-trained classifiers on these new “site-balanced test sets” and found that the accuracies did not differ significantly from the original test set results: here, it was 69.88% for ADHD-200 and 63.46% for ABIDE." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_0a18ed38 full_text sha256:c45b568564aed9a2ce5c1559ce50c6a119000557051d641a0d3cc5a393d3dcae section:results (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "Accuracy on site-balanced (50:50 case:control per site) test sets was 63.46% for ABIDE, not significantly different from the original test set, confirming the result is not a site-composition artifact." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-023/7> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "Both datasets are available online publicly. The ADHD-200 dataset is available at: http://fcon_1000.projects.nitrc.org/ indi/adhd200/ The ABIDE dataset is available at: (http://fcon_1000.projects.nitrc.org/indi/abide/)." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0194856> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_0a18ed38 full_text sha256:c45b568564aed9a2ce5c1559ce50c6a119000557051d641a0d3cc5a393d3dcae section:methods (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
