    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "200 ROIs were derived from the Craddock atlas to compute connectivity matrices." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-029/4> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value """Data presented in this study underwent standard fMRI pre-
processing (i.e., realignment, normalization, and smoothing) 
implemented in SPM12b. Data were preprocessed according to 
standard SPM protocols including realignment, normalization 
to a study specific template using DARTEL, smoothing, band-
pass filtering (0.01–0.05 Hz), and scrubbing to account for head 
movements (63).""" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-1> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2016.00177> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_f02fbc88 full_text sha256:c5817ba94862aa63dfd28b3519a78ce82b4824d9daa7b1f3685c3b10d8b257e5 section:methods char:71523" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "Data were preprocessed with SPM12 (realignment, DARTEL normalization, smoothing, band-pass filtering, motion scrubbing)." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-029/5> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value """The performance of each classifier is assessed by nested cross-
validation: 10-folds are used in the outer cross-validation loop for 
the performance estimation, and 10-folds are used in the inner 
cross-validation loop to determine the optimal threshold value 
t for feature selection, or the optimal regularization parameter 
for lasso-regularized""" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-1> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2016.00177> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_f02fbc88 full_text sha256:c5817ba94862aa63dfd28b3519a78ce82b4824d9daa7b1f3685c3b10d8b257e5 section:methods char:39420" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "Nested 10x10-fold cross-validation was used: outer loop for performance estimation, inner loop for feature-selection/tuning-parameter selection." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-029/6> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value """One pitfall is given when feature 
selection or selection of tuning parameters is performed on the full 
data, i.e., on data samples from both the training and the test set.""" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-1> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2016.00177> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_f02fbc88 full_text sha256:c5817ba94862aa63dfd28b3519a78ce82b4824d9daa7b1f3685c3b10d8b257e5 section:results char:40850" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "The paper explicitly identifies the 'peeking'/double-dipping pitfall of performing feature selection on the full dataset rather than training data only." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-029/7> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value """If, however, we use the entire dataset to select the 
features with a mean difference above a threshold value t = 0.10, 
classification with a linear SVM yields a test accuracy of 91%. If 
the feature selection is correctly applied using only the training 


9
Kassraian-Fard et al.
Classification of Psychiatric Imaging Data 
Frontiers in Psychiatry  |  www.frontiersin.org
December 2016  |  Volume 7  |  Article 177
set, the classification accuracy is between 45 and 56%.""" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-1> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2016.00177> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_f02fbc88 full_text sha256:c5817ba94862aa63dfd28b3519a78ce82b4824d9daa7b1f3685c3b10d8b257e5 section:results char:41358" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "A simulation shows that incorrect (whole-dataset) feature selection can inflate accuracy to 91% versus 45-56% when feature selection is correctly confined to the training set." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-029/8> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value """We took the so far best performing classifier – the support 
vector machine – and applied it to the data set after this stand-
ardization was performed. The resulting classification accuracy 
increased from 63 to 68%.""" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-1> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2016.00177> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_f02fbc88 full_text sha256:c5817ba94862aa63dfd28b3519a78ce82b4824d9daa7b1f3685c3b10d8b257e5 section:results char:43986" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "Per-site z-standardization (train-only mean/SD) improved the best classifier's (SVM) accuracy from 63% to 68%." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-029/9> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value """Another possibility to assess the generalizability of the clas-
sifier to data from different sites is to form training and test sets 
from different sites. An example of this approach is leave-one-
site-out cross-validation, where the test set contains data from a 
site that has not been used in the training set (36).""" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-1> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2016.00177> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_f02fbc88 full_text sha256:c5817ba94862aa63dfd28b3519a78ce82b4824d9daa7b1f3685c3b10d8b257e5 section:discussion char:44476" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "Leave-one-site-out cross-validation is described as an approach to assess generalizability across sites." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-030/1> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "We attained results competitive on this task for a combined ABIDE-I and II datasets of ~66%. When all summary measures were combined the result was still only as good as that of the best single measure which was regional homogeneity (ReHo)." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00440> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_97b1be33 full_text sha256:18732a88a9b397517bf8f3908a94113e90b7091a1d5b8a88755220fb4c3a48dc section:abstract (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "The 3D-CNN achieved ~66% accuracy on the combined ABIDE I+II dataset; combining all summary measures performed no better than the best single measure (ReHo)." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-030/2> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "The ABIDE I+II datasets is a collection of structural (T1w) and functional (rs-fMRI) brain images aggregated across 29 institutions (10), available for download2. It includes 1,028 participants with a diagnosis of autism, Asperger or pervasive developmental disorder-not otherwise speciﬁed (called ASD from now on), and 1,141 typically developing participants (CON)." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00440> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_97b1be33 full_text sha256:18732a88a9b397517bf8f3908a94113e90b7091a1d5b8a88755220fb4c3a48dc section:methods (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "ABIDE I+II aggregates data from 29 institutions, with 1,028 ASD and 1,141 typically developing participants in the full release." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-030/3> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "We chose to cut off the minimum scan duration to 100-time points, which led us to include 96% of the whole ABIDE I+II dataset (N=2,085, N(ASD) =993), the vast majority of which (95%) with a minimum acquisition time of 4 min." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00440> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_97b1be33 full_text sha256:18732a88a9b397517bf8f3908a94113e90b7091a1d5b8a88755220fb4c3a48dc section:methods (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "A minimum scan-duration cutoff of 100 time points retained 96% of ABIDE I+II (N=2,085, N(ASD)=993)." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-030/4> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "The preprocessing was done using the Conﬁgurable Pipeline for the Analysis of Connectomes (C-PAC, (12). We followed a preprocessing strategy adopted by the Preprocessed Connectome Project initiative3. This will allow others to replicate and extend the ﬁndings in this paper." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00440> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_97b1be33 full_text sha256:18732a88a9b397517bf8f3908a94113e90b7091a1d5b8a88755220fb4c3a48dc section:methods (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "Preprocessing used C-PAC following a Preprocessed Connectomes Project strategy, chosen explicitly to enable replication." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-030/5> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "For the leave-site-out CV procedure, we selected ﬁve sites with the highest number of total subjects (ASD/total), namely New York University (NYU) (90/159), Kennedy Krieger Institute - 1 (KKI-I) (88/114), University of Miami - 1 (UM-I) (50/96), University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA)-I (28/69), Oregon Health & Science University (OHSU)-I (42/64)." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00440> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_97b1be33 full_text sha256:18732a88a9b397517bf8f3908a94113e90b7091a1d5b8a88755220fb4c3a48dc section:methods (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "The leave-site-out evaluation used the five largest sites (NYU, KKI-I, UM-I, UCLA-I, OHSU-I) with each held out as the test set in turn." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-030/6> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "When assessed by ﬁve-fold CV procedure, all tested models performed at around 60% accuracy for the classiﬁcation task (Figure 2 and Table 2), with little variation between models' performances. On the contrary, the leave-site-out CV procedure shows high variability in terms of model performances with relatively good performance for the NYU site and poor performance for the other sites" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00440> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_97b1be33 full_text sha256:18732a88a9b397517bf8f3908a94113e90b7091a1d5b8a88755220fb4c3a48dc section:results (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "Five-fold CV gave around 60% accuracy for all models with little variation, while leave-site-out CV showed high variability, good for NYU and poor for other sites." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-030/7> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
    prov:value "The overall best performing model was the MM-ensemble, which achieved balanced accuracy of 64% and F1 score of 66%, averaged over the ﬁve-folds of the CV procedure. With the leave- site-out CV procedure the performance of the MM-ensemble dropped to an average balanced accuracy of mean 56% and F1 score of 59%, suggesting that this model does not do well in generalizing to new sites." ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/charting-batch-3> ;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2020.00440> ;
    ex:sourceLocator "corpus local_97b1be33 full_text sha256:18732a88a9b397517bf8f3908a94113e90b7091a1d5b8a88755220fb4c3a48dc section:results (whitespace/ligature-normalised match)" ;
    ex:sourceQuoteVerified true ;
    ex:supportsClaim "The best model (MM-ensemble) reached 64% balanced accuracy / 66% F1 under 5-fold CV, dropping to 56% balanced accuracy / 59% F1 under leave-site-out CV." ;
    ex:verifiedBy <urn:repronim:abide:litreview/activity/phase3-merge> .

<urn:repronim:abide:litreview/quote/S-030/8> a prov:Entity,
        ex:EvidenceQuote ;
